// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0
// © Ilai - Asset Divergence Detector (PCP / PSP) v5.37
// Pine Script V5
//
// v5.37 — the fast box works in Bar Replay again, and a PCP that can no
//  longer become a swing stops being announced.
//  v5.35 limited the fast 5m/15m/1m readers to their last 100 bars
//  (calc_bars_count). In Bar Replay those are the last 100 bars of the real
//  data, not of the replay point, so on a 5m chart the 15m row was empty —
//  no PSP, no PCP — and on a 15m chart the 5m row was. The limit is gone; it
//  never changed the series count anyway.
//  A pending PCP — a candle that closed with a divergence, waiting for the
//  next close to decide its swing — is only worth showing while it can still
//  BE a swing. It is now dropped, everywhere (the fast box, the ◦ in the line,
//  the dot on the chart), the moment no asset that takes part can make it
//  one: on each of them the candle was not above (below) the one before it,
//  or the candle forming now has already gone past its high (low). The
//  stepped timeframes read "gone past" off the wick, so under the close rule
//  only the first half applies there.
//  Free: the flags ride in the swing number each request already returns.
//
// v5.36 — Q1 / blocked becomes a setting, and "own" means part of the break.
//  One switch, three states, for a PSP born in the first quarter of its
//  container or in a blocked time:
//   · "בצבע נפרד" — what v5.34 did: an ordinary PSP everywhere, in the Q1 colour.
//   · "רגיל"      — an ordinary PSP everywhere, in its ordinary colour.
//   · "לא קיים"   — it never enters anything: no marker, no line, no stack, no
//     fast box, no alert, no hub. An older break underneath stays on display.
//  A solid ("own") triad marker needed only a swing on the chart's symbol, so
//  on an RTY chart — or any chart outside the triad — a triad PCP plus an RTY
//  swing drew a full triad PSP although RTY is not in the triad, and on a YM
//  chart a YM swing counted even when only NQ and ES diverged. The chart's
//  swing now counts as the triad's own only when the chart is an asset that
//  takes part: 1 or 2 when included, 3 only when 3 is the one that diverged —
//  exactly the rule the faded ("ext") markers already used. The 3–4 pair is
//  unchanged: a pair PSP still shows on every chart, solid on 3 and 4, faded
//  on 1 and 2.
//  Sunday (crypto only) now belongs to the week before it, as in the SSMT and
//  Fill indicators. Futures are unaffected — Sunday 18:00 is already Monday.
//  The breaks line in the corner is drawn in the tiny text size.
//
// v5.35 — it compiles, and it uses far less memory.
//  v5.34 gave asset 4's per-timeframe objects the names r1h, r4h, r1d, r1w
//  and rCh — the same names the line's text cells already used. Every one
//  was a redefinition, and every later use failed with it. The objects are
//  z1h, z4h, z1d, z1w, zCh (and z15, z5m on the fast side) now.
//  Memory, for Bar Replay months back:
//   · max_bars_back = 5000 is gone. It forced a 5000-bar history buffer on
//     EVERY variable in the script; nothing here looks back more than three
//     bars, and Pine sizes the buffers itself when it is not set.
//   · Two candle directions travel as one number (d1*4 + d2), and the two
//     swing flags as one number, so a stepped request is 7 series instead of
//     9 and a fast one 2 instead of 3. 193 series → 150 (asset 4 off: ~115).
//   · The fast 5m/15m/1m readers compute only their last 100 bars — they are
//     only ever read on the last bar.
//  Nothing in the detection changed.
//
// v5.34 — four assets chosen by hand, a 3–4 pair, and Q1/blocked as a colour.
//  Assets: four input.symbol fields replace the automatic contract set. The
//  role comes from the position — 1 and 2 are the strong pair that decides,
//  3 is the weak one, 4 is 3's partner — and every label is read off the
//  symbol itself (MNQ1! → NQ, M2K1! → RTY, MGC1! → GC), so gold or crypto
//  read right. Asset 4 is optional; switched off, its requests are asset 3's.
//  The 3–4 pair is a divergence of its own: 3 and 4 close in opposite
//  directions on a candle that is a swing on either. The two are equals, so
//  the break lives until both have crossed that candle's extreme, under the
//  same containers as everything else. It has its own stacks, its own colour,
//  its own cell in the line and its own rows in the 5m/15m box. Its names
//  never include asset 1 or 2, and a triad break always does — that is what
//  tells the two apart at a glance.
//  A PSP born in the first quarter of its container, or in a blocked time
//  (Friday on 1H; Friday of week 4, week 5 and a dead week on 4H), is now an
//  ordinary PSP in every way — line, box, alert, hub — drawn in its own
//  colour. That replaces the grey dot. The first quarter counts on every
//  ladder: the first 22.5 minutes of a micro on 1m, the first 90 minutes of a
//  session on 5m, Asia on 15m, Monday on 1H, week 1 on 4H, the first
//  quarter-of-quarter on 1D, April–June on 1W, year 1 of the cycle on 1Mo.
//  Removed: the panel with its debug rows, the "broken" alert — an alert now
//  fires on a new break only — and everything only they used. Markers are kept
//  as data through history and drawn once, on the last bar.
//
// v5.33 — 1H and 4H are never muted; only their container ends them.
//  v5.30 drew a Friday PSP on 1H, and a 4H PSP on a Friday, in a dead week or
//  in week 1, as a plain dot and kept it out of the line. That was wrong for
//  how these are traded: a PSP on either timeframe is an ordinary PSP, alive
//  until it is taken or its container ends — the week on 1H, the month on 4H.
//  Daily and weekly keep their muting unchanged.
//
// v5.32 — YM counts on the 1m chart too, under the strength rule only.
//  It was switched off on 1m altogether. It now takes part exactly as on 5m
//  and 15m: YM up while ES and/or NQ are down is a divergence. Weakness stays
//  daily-and-above, so on 1m it cannot fire. The chart's own engine already
//  read YM on 1m; this brings the markers in line with it.
//
// v5.31 — the 5m/15m box names who is STILL HOLDING the swing, and only that.
//  The box read the PSP off the last closed bar and never looked again, so
//  once a wick took the swing candle's extreme it went on announcing a PSP
//  that, on the chart you were looking at, was already gone. Its names were
//  the assets that had diverged, not the ones still defending.
//  Each request now also reports, per asset, whether the swing candle's
//  extreme has been crossed since — by the confirming bar or by the one still
//  forming — and the box applies the line's own rule: names are the assets
//  still defending, NQ and ES decide, YM never does. A PSP nobody is holding
//  any more is not shown. Free: the two flags ride inside the number that
//  already carried the swing (+4 high taken, +8 low taken). Still 138 series.
//
// v5.30 — Quarterly Theory decides how long a PSP lives and whether it counts.
//  Every timeframe compares the quarters of a larger cycle — its container —
//  and when the container rolls, everything resets. So a break now carries
//  the container it was born in and dies when that container ends, taken or
//  not: 1m a 90-minute micro, 5m a 6-hour session, 15m a trading day, 1H a
//  week, 4H a month (a week belongs to its Tuesday's month), 1D a QT quarter,
//  1W a QT year (April to March). New York time, the day opening at 18:00.
//  A PSP born where its timeframe cannot carry a break — Friday on 1H and 4H,
//  a dead week on 4H, and the first quarter of a container that has no seed
//  (4H week 1, the first quarter-of-quarter on 1D, April–June on 1W) — never
//  enters the line and is drawn as a plain dot instead of a marker. The dot
//  stays until it is taken or its container ends; it never becomes a PSP.
//  Cost: none. The clock each request carried, time_close[1], becomes time[2]
//  — the swing candle's own open, which moves exactly when the old clock did
//  and is also the birth time the container is read from. Still 138 series.
//  Also: one list of shapes, and a PSP on another asset now has exactly the
//  same shape as one on the chart's own — only the fade tells them apart.
//  The debug panel gains a row with the birth date of each timeframe's break
//  on display, so "which candle is this?" is one screenshot.
//
// v5.29 — the marker sits where you tell it to, not where yloc decides.
//  yloc.abovebar leaves a gap that grows with the label's size, so making the
//  markers readable in v5.28 pushed them away from the candles. The label is
//  priced now — high[1] plus a gap, low[1] minus it — and the gap is an input
//  measured as a percentage of ATR, which means the same spacing on NQ as on
//  YM and on a 5m chart as on a weekly one. 0 puts it on the wick itself.
//
// v5.28 — the marker has a size and a shape you choose.
//  Moving to labels in v5.25 left the glyph and the size hard-coded, and
//  size.tiny on a label is smaller than the same name was on a plotchar.
//  Two inputs now: five sizes, and five shapes — full triangle, the small
//  triangle this had, circle, diamond, or two characters you type yourself.
//  Filled still means the swing was on the chart's own asset and hollow means
//  it was on another, so the one thing the marker always told you survives
//  every shape. Drawing only; nothing here decides anything.
//
// v5.27 — one engine per timeframe, so "1H" says the same thing everywhere.
//  On a 5m chart the 1H entry came from the stepped engine. On a 1H chart
//  3600 > 3600 is false, so that entry was hidden and the chart's own engine
//  took its place under the same "1H" label — a different engine, built from
//  a different series over a different history. Two answers for one
//  timeframe, and which one you got depended on where you were standing.
//  The listed timeframes now come from the stepped engine whenever they are
//  at or above the chart, and the chart's own entry appears only when it is
//  not already one of them. Requesting a timeframe equal to the chart's is
//  safe in a way requesting a lower one is not: one sample per chart bar is
//  exactly one bar of that timeframe, nothing is skipped.
//  Nothing in the detection changed. This is which of two existing answers
//  the line shows.
//
// v5.26 — who decides that a marker is taken is now a setting.
//  v5.25 handed the markers the breaks line's rule: NQ and ES both have to
//  cross before anything is erased. On a chart that is one of them, that rule
//  keeps markers you can see were traded through — your eyes are on NQ, the
//  marker is waiting on ES as well.
//  A marker is a chart object sitting on a candle in front of you, so the
//  default is now the simple thing: once THIS chart has traded through that
//  candle's own extreme, the marker goes. The stricter rules are still there
//  for anyone who wants the markers and the line to say the same thing.
//  Only the erasing changed. Which candles get marked in the first place is
//  the same code it was.
//
// v5.25 — a marker whose candle was taken is erased from the chart.
//  plotchar cannot do this. Its value for a historical bar is frozen the
//  moment that bar is processed, and "taken later" is future information
//  there. The four PSP markers become labels, which can be deleted, and each
//  one carries the same Brk the breaks line uses — the swing candle's extreme
//  on each asset — so it is judged by exactly the same rule: NQ and ES decide,
//  YM never does, a level erased as it falls.
//  What this costs, and it is not nothing: Pine allows at most 500 label
//  objects, so markers are only drawn over a window of recent bars, 200 by
//  default. Older history shows nothing at all. That is the trade for being
//  able to erase, and the window is an input.
//  The ◦ pending dots stay plotchar — they only ever sit on the unfinished bar
//  and clear themselves when it closes, so they never need deleting.
//
// v5.24 — the ◦ carries its own timeframe, "◦4H".
//  Giving it a cell of its own fixed the colour and broke the reading: in
//  "1W ▲ NQ ES ◦ 1D ▼ ALL ◦" there is nothing to say whether a ◦ belongs to
//  the entry before it or the one after. Two characters settle it.
//
// v5.23 — the ◦ gets a cell of its own, so it can be its own colour.
//  A standing break and a candle waiting on its swing verdict are two
//  unrelated things, and v5.18 put them in one cell. A Pine table cell carries
//  a single text colour, so the ◦ came out red beside a bearish break and read
//  as part of it — the exact confusion it was added to prevent.
//  It is now a separate cell, always in the pending colour, whatever the break
//  beside it is doing. The line goes to twelve columns to make room; columns
//  cost nothing and empty ones render as nothing.
//
// v5.22 — the pending ◦ is black, not washed-out grey.
//  #9e9e9e at 25% transparency all but disappeared on a light chart. Black
//  and opaque by default; it is an input, so a dark theme wants it changed.
//  One thing it cannot fix: a ◦ riding next to a LIVE break shares that
//  break's cell, and a Pine table cell carries a single text colour, so there
//  it comes out in the break's colour. Splitting it into a cell of its own
//  would cost a column in the line.
//
// v5.21 — every asset defends the candle, and NQ+ES decide:
//  The real fault was upstream of the majority rule. A level was stored only
//  for an asset that MADE the swing, so a break born off a YM swing alone had
//  no level on NQ or ES at all — and an asset with no level can never take
//  anything. NQ and ES could be long past that candle and the break lived on,
//  not because they were holding it, but because nobody was watching them.
//  The swing now decides only WHICH CANDLE and WHICH DIRECTION. After that
//  every enabled asset defends that candle's own extreme on its own chart,
//  and the break dies once NQ and ES have both taken it. YM is tracked and
//  named in the line, and never decides — unless NQ and ES are both switched
//  off, where there is nobody else to ask.
//  Making no swing there means nothing either way: an asset that never swung
//  but has not crossed that candle's extreme is still defending it, and that
//  is exactly why the hourly YM-only PSP stays valid while the other two have
//  not gone past. Only an actual crossing counts.
//  hi2 and lo2 are already fetched for all three assets, so this costs no
//  extra request.security. Still 138 series across 21 calls.
//  The "YM alone" special case is gone with it — it existed only because a
//  YM-born break had no other level to count.
//
// v5.20 — a majority decides, and the line names who is still defending:
//  v5.17 let a break live while ANY asset that made it still held its level.
//  That fixed YM killing breaks on its own and created the mirror fault: the
//  Dow often has nothing to do with the other two, so its swing survives while
//  both of theirs are taken, and the break rides on YM alone.
//  A break now dies once a MAJORITY of the levels it was born with is gone,
//  and never rides on YM alone — unless YM was the only asset that ever held a
//  level for it, in which case there is no majority to speak of.
//  The names in the line change meaning with it: they used to say who made the
//  divergence, fixed at birth. They now say who is STILL DEFENDING, so
//  "4H ▼ NQ ES" becomes "4H ▼ ES" the moment NQ's level is taken, and you can
//  read what is holding the break up without opening anything.
//  Note what that costs: a level is only stored for an asset that made the
//  SWING, not for every asset that diverged, so the list is shorter than the
//  old one by design. It is the honest answer to "what is keeping this alive".
//
// v5.19 — YM weakness moves up to daily and above.
//  It was 4H and above. 4H now joins 1H in never carrying it, so the rule
//  lives on 1D and 1W only, and on the chart's own bars only when the chart
//  is daily or higher.
//
// v5.18 — two things that were both "it is not showing what I can see":
//
//  1. A break was only ever tested against the last CLOSED bar of its
//     timeframe. On a 4H chart that means you watch price blow through a
//     swing high and the engine keeps the break alive for up to four hours.
//     A level is taken the moment price reaches it, closed bar or not.
//     This costs NO extra request.security: the running high and low of the
//     bar still forming can be accumulated from the CHART's own bars, which
//     are already fetched for all three assets. The accumulator resets when
//     that timeframe's clock rolls, so it always covers exactly the bar in
//     progress. Still 138 series across 21 calls.
//     Wick-based only — with the close rule an unfinished bar has no close
//     to test, so that setting keeps the old behaviour untouched.
//
//  2. The early warning was in the code and unreachable. f_rec read
//     "live ? break : pending ? ◦ : nothing", so the grey ◦ — a bar that
//     closed with a divergence and is waiting on its swing verdict — could
//     only ever appear on a timeframe with NO standing break. Exactly the
//     timeframes you watch always have one. The ◦ now rides alongside a live
//     break instead of being hidden by it.
//
// v5.17 — one asset could kill a break the others were still holding:
//  The invalidation test was an OR across the three levels, so whichever asset
//  took its own level first killed the whole break. In practice that asset was
//  usually YM — the smallest and noisiest of the three — wiping out bearish
//  breaks whose swing highs NQ and ES had never gone near. That is why the
//  line kept falling back to an older bullish break: the newer bearish ones
//  were being removed by YM alone.
//  A break now survives while ANY asset that made it still defends its level.
//  The level each asset took is erased as it is taken, and the break dies only
//  when the last one is gone — which also fixes the half of this that an OR
//  could never express: the test only ever sees the bar that just closed, so a
//  level taken last week and another taken today would never have been true at
//  the same moment. Erasing them as they fall is what accumulates.
//  One input to go back to the old reading, off by default.
//
// v5.16 — the debug panel shows the stacks themselves (removed in v5.34).
//
// v5.15 — a wick through the level kills the break:
//  The switch was already there and defaulted to the other reading: only a
//  CLOSE beyond the swing level counted, so a bar that pierced the level and
//  came back left the break standing. The level is the thing being defended,
//  and touching it is taking it. Default flipped; the old behaviour is one
//  checkbox away.
//
// v5.14 — a timeframe remembers more than one break:
//  Each timeframe held exactly ONE break, and a new PSP overwrote it. So a
//  fresh PSP that got taken straight away wiped out an older one whose level
//  had never been touched, and the timeframe went blank — or worse, showed a
//  direction that no longer matched anything on the chart.
//  Each timeframe now keeps a small stack of breaks, newest first. Every close
//  tests EVERY stored break against its own level and its own direction, and
//  drops the ones that were taken; the one on display is simply the newest
//  survivor. Take out the new one and the previous one comes back, exactly as
//  long as it is still untaken. Depth is an input, default 5.
//  The levels moved into the stacked break where they belong — one break, one
//  set of levels — so the separate Lv type is gone.
//
// v5.13 — a hue for YM weakness, because dimness is already spoken for:
//  v5.12 drew it in the same colour, faded. That collides: a faded marker
//  already means "the swing was on another asset, not the one on your chart",
//  so two different things would have arrived as the same visual signal and
//  a faded-and-hollow marker would have been unreadable. Weakness goes back to
//  its own colour, amber by default — hue says WHICH RULE fired, dimness still
//  says WHERE the swing was, and the two stay independent.
//
//  Worth stating since it is the other half of the question: YM weakness never
//  overrides a normal divergence. It is tested only after ES-vs-NQ and YM
//  strength have both come up empty, so a bar where ES and NQ already disagree
//  is an ordinary break in ordinary colours, whatever YM did on it.
//
// v5.11 — YM weakness is a category at all: YM DOWN while the others are up,
//  tested only after ES-vs-NQ and YM strength both come up empty. It was 4H
//  and above when introduced; v5.19 moved it to daily and above.
// v5.10 — the breaks line is 1H and above, full stop; the chart's own
//  timeframe joins it only when the chart is 1H or higher.
// v5.9 — the 5m/15m heads-up gets a box of its own, PCP included, plus a real
//  alert(). NOTE: alert() delivers nothing until an alert is created on the
//  indicator in TradingView with the condition "Any alert() function call".
// v5.8 — CME futures default to the SETTLEMENT price as the daily close and a
//  chart's per-symbol override never reaches request.security, so the script
//  was reading a different candle than the one on screen. ticker.modify fixes
//  it; the setting defaults to OFF, matching a chart with the box unticked.
// v5.6 — each timeframe's clock rides INSIDE its request tuple. Timing it from
//  the built-in time_close(tf) desynchronises it from the data it times.
// v5.5 — "Memory limits exceeded" is a LOAD-time failure that compiles clean.
//  Every tuple element of every request.security is a full series held over
//  the chart's history, and the budget is shared with every other indicator on
//  the chart. 210 series failed. Keep the tuples small.
// v5.4..v5.0 — the chart's own timeframe needs no request at all; the line
//  lists every standing break side by side; "live" is a flag of its own so dir
//  and who survive an invalidation.
// v4.x — YM strength rule; swings detected on every included asset (solid
//  marker = swing on the chart symbol, hollow = on another asset only);
//  pending dot; weekly as a full category; three input.symbol fields.

//@version=5
indicator("Asset Divergence | PCP & PSP v5", shorttitle="ADI v5",
     overlay          = true,
     max_labels_count = 500)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  INPUTS
//  Hebrew labels. Every option string below is also compared in code —
//  translating one without the other silently breaks the setting.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

grp_mode   = "═══  זיהוי  ═══"
i_ignore_doji = input.bool(false, title="התעלם מדוג'י (סגירה = פתיחה)",
     tooltip="כבוי (ברירת מחדל): דוג'י נחשב כיוון שונה ויכול ליצור PCP.\nדלוק: דוג'י ניטרלי ולעולם לא יוצר PCP.",
     group=grp_mode)

grp_assets = "═══  נכסים  ═══"
// Four symbols chosen by hand. The role is the position: 1 and 2 are the
// strong pair and decide, 3 is the weak one, 4 is 3's partner.
i_sym1     = input.symbol("CME_MINI:MNQ1!",  title="נכס 1 (חזק)",  group=grp_assets)
i_sym2     = input.symbol("CME_MINI:MES1!",  title="נכס 2 (חזק)",  group=grp_assets)
i_sym3     = input.symbol("CBOT_MINI:MYM1!", title="נכס 3 (חלש)",  group=grp_assets)
i_sym4     = input.symbol("CME_MINI:M2K1!",  title="נכס 4 (בן הזוג של 3)", group=grp_assets)
i_use4     = input.bool(true, title="כלול נכס 4 — זוג 3–4",
     tooltip="דלוק: נכסים 3 ו-4 הם זוג שווה. PSP של הזוג = השניים נסגרים בכיוונים הפוכים על נר שהוא סווינג באחד מהם. מוצג בצבע משלו, ומת כששניהם חצו את הקצה של אותו נר.\nכבוי: לזהב ולקריפטו, שיש להם רק 3 נכסים. הבקשות של נכס 4 שוות לנכס 3 ולא עולות זיכרון.",
     group=grp_assets)
i_adjust   = input.string("בלי יישור", title="נתוני חוזה רציף",
     options=["בלי יישור", "מיושר לגלגול", "ברירת המחדל של הסימבול"],
     tooltip="ברירת המחדל: בלי יישור. בשבוע גלגול חוזים כדאי לעבור ל'מיושר לגלגול'.",
     group=grp_assets)
i_use_nq   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול נכס 1", group=grp_assets)
i_use_es   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול נכס 2", group=grp_assets)
i_use_ym   = input.bool(true,  title="כלול נכס 3",
     tooltip="חוזקה: נכס 3 נסגר בעלייה בזמן ש-1 ו/או 2 נסגרים בירידה.\nכבוי מכבה גם את הזוג 3–4.",
     group=grp_assets)
i_ym_weak  = input.bool(true, title="כלול גם חולשת נכס 3 (יומי ומעלה)",
     tooltip="נכס 3 נסגר בירידה בזמן ש-1 ו-2 נסגרים בעלייה. מצויר בצבע נפרד.\nנספר רק כשאין כבר דיברגנס אחר — אם 1 ו-2 חלוקים ביניהם, זו שבירה רגילה בצבע רגיל.\nפעיל רק על נרות יומיים ומעלה.",
     group=grp_assets)
i_settle   = input.string("כבוי — כמו הגרף", title="Settlement כסגירה יומית",
     options=["כבוי — כמו הגרף", "דלוק", "ברירת המחדל של הסימבול"],
     tooltip="בחוזי CME ברירת המחדל היא שהסגירה היומית היא מחיר הסילוק, לא הסגירה הרגילה.\nהגדרת הגרף שלך לא עוברת ל-request.security, ולכן בלי זה הסקריפט קורא נר אחר ממה שאתה רואה.\nהשאר על 'כבוי' אם ההגדרה בגרף לא מסומנת.",
     group=grp_assets)

grp_tf     = "═══  מסגרת הגרף  ═══"
i_tf_1m    = input.bool(true,  title="1m",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_5m    = input.bool(true,  title="5m",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_15m   = input.bool(true,  title="15m",    group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1h    = input.bool(true,  title="1H",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_4h    = input.bool(true,  title="4H",     group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1d    = input.bool(true,  title="יומי",   group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1w    = input.bool(true,  title="שבועי",  group=grp_tf)
i_tf_1mo   = input.bool(true,  title="חודשי",  group=grp_tf,
     tooltip="PSP בין שנים, בתוך מחזור 4 שנים קלנדרי (2023–2026, 2027–2030).")

grp_col    = "═══  סימונים וצבעים  ═══"
i_col_bull = input.color(color.new(#00e5ff, 0), title="אות שורי", group=grp_col)
i_col_bear = input.color(color.new(#ff1744, 0), title="אות דובי", group=grp_col)
i_col_weak = input.color(color.new(#ff9100, 0), title="אות חולשת נכס 3",
     tooltip="צבע נפרד, לא עמעום — עמעום כבר תפוס לסימון שהסווינג קרה בנכס אחר.",
     group=grp_col)
i_col_pair = input.color(color.new(#00c853, 0), title="אות זוג 3–4",
     tooltip="צבע אחיד לשני הכיוונים — הכיוון ידוע מהמיקום מעל או מתחת לנר ומהחץ בשורה.",
     group=grp_col)
i_col_q1   = input.color(color.new(#aa00ff, 0), title="אות ברבע ראשון / זמן חסום",
     tooltip="PSP שנולד ברבע הראשון של המיכל שלו, או בזמן חסום (שישי ב-1H; שישי של שבוע 4, שבוע 5 ושבוע מת ב-4H).\nחל רק כשההגדרה 'PSP ברבע ראשון / זמן חסום' היא 'בצבע נפרד'. גובר על שאר הצבעים.",
     group=grp_col)
i_ext_transp = input.int(45, title="עמעום סימון של נכס אחר", minval=0, maxval=90,
     tooltip="כשהסווינג קרה בנכס אחר ולא בסימבול שעל הגרף, הסימון יוצא באותה צורה בדיוק — רק שקוף יותר. זה המספר.",
     group=grp_col)
i_show_pending = input.bool(true, title="הצג סימון PCP ממתין (•)",
     tooltip="נר PCP מוכרע רק כשהנר שאחריו נסגר. עד אז הוא מסומן בנקודה.\nהנקודה נעלמת ברגע שהנר כבר לא יכול להיות סווינג — הנר שאחריו עבר את הגבוה (הנמוך) שלו בכל נכס שמשתתף.",
     group=grp_col)
i_col_pend = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), title="צבע PCP ממתין",
     tooltip="צובע את ה-◦ בשורה וגם את הנקודות על הנרות.\nשחור ואטום כברירת מחדל, כי אפור שקוף נבלע בגרף בהיר. על ערכת נושא כהה תחליף לבן.",
     group=grp_col)
i_mark_sz = input.string("רגיל", title="גודל הסימון",
     options=["זעיר", "קטן", "רגיל", "גדול", "ענק"], group=grp_col)
i_mark_gl = input.string("משולש גדול ▲", title="צורת הסימון",
     options=["משולש גדול ▲", "משולש קטן ▴", "עיגול ●", "נקודה •", "ריבוע ■", "יהלום ◆", "חץ ⬇", "כוכב ★", "איקס ✕", "טקסט משלי"],
     tooltip="אותה צורה לסווינג בנכס שעל הגרף ולסווינג בנכס אחר — ההבדל היחיד הוא העמעום.\nמשולשים: ▲ מעל נר דובי, ▼ מתחת לנר שורי. חץ: מצביע אל הנר.",
     group=grp_col)
i_mark_tx_bear = input.string("▲", title="טקסט משלי — דובי (מעל הנר)", group=grp_col)
i_mark_tx_bull = input.string("▼", title="טקסט משלי — שורי (מתחת לנר)", group=grp_col)
i_mark_gap = input.int(15, title="מרחק הסימון מהנר (% מ-ATR)", minval=0, maxval=300,
     tooltip="נמדד כאחוז מה-ATR ולא בנקודות, כדי שאותו מספר ייתן אותו מרווח על כל נכס ועל כל מסגרת זמן.\n0 = הסימון יושב על הפתיל עצמו.",
     group=grp_col)
i_mark_erase = input.bool(true, title="מחק סימון שנלקח מהנרות",
     tooltip="כשהנר שמתחת לסימון נלקח — לפי הכלל שנבחר למטה — הסימון נמחק מהמסך.\nכבוי: הסימונים נשארים עד שהם יוצאים מחלון הסימון.",
     group=grp_col)
i_mark_rule = input.string("הנכס של הגרף", title="מתי סימון נחשב נלקח",
     options=["הנכס של הגרף", "שני המכריעים", "כל הנכסים"],
     tooltip="הנכס של הגרף: ברגע שהגרף שאתה עליו עבר את הקצה של אותו נר. זה מה שהעין רואה.\nשני המכריעים: החוק של השורה — נכסים 1 ו-2 (ובזוג: 3 ו-4) צריכים לעבור.\nכל הנכסים: גם נכס 3 צריך לעבור. הכי שמרני.",
     group=grp_col)
i_mark_keep = input.int(200, title="חלון סימון (סימונים אחורה)", minval=20, maxval=450,
     tooltip="פיין מרשה 500 אובייקטים בלבד, ולכן נשמרים רק הסימונים האחרונים. ישנים יותר לא מסומנים.",
     group=grp_col)
i_show_pcp_bars = input.bool(false, title="צבע את כל נרות ה-PCP", group=grp_col)
i_col_pcp  = input.color(color.new(#ffd54f, 80), title="גוון נרות PCP", group=grp_col)

grp_mtf    = "═══  מסגרות זמן גבוהות  ═══"
i_mtf_on   = input.bool(true, title="הצג שורת שבירות",
     tooltip="שורה אחת בפינה: השבירה העומדת בכל מסגרת, והשמות הם מי שעדיין מגן עליה.\nלידה ◦ עם שם המסגרת — נר שנסגר עם דיברגנס ומחכה לסגירה הבאה.\nאחריהן תא בצבע הזוג — שבירה של 3–4. השמות בו אף פעם לא כוללים את 1 או 2.\nמוצגות רק מסגרות גבוהות ממסגרת הגרף או שוות לה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_v    = input.string("למטה", title="גובה השורה",
     options=["למעלה", "באמצע", "למטה"], group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_h    = input.string("שמאל", title="צד השורה",
     options=["שמאל", "מרכז", "ימין"], group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_pad  = input.int(0, title="הרחקת השורה מהקצה (שורות)", minval=0, maxval=12,
     tooltip="מוסיף שורות ריקות בין השורה לקצה הגרף, כדי להרים אותה מעל שורה של אינדיקטור אחר שיושב באותה פינה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_depth    = input.int(5, title="כמה שבירות לזכור לכל מסגרת", minval=1, maxval=10,
     tooltip="שבירה חדשה לא מוחקת את הקודמת. אם החדשה נלקחת, חוזרים להצגת הקודמת — כל עוד הרמה שלה עצמה לא נלקחה.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_kill_all = input.bool(true, title="ביטול לפי שני המכריעים",
     tooltip="דלוק (ברירת מחדל): הסווינג קובע איזה נר ואיזה כיוון, ואז כל נכס מגן על הקצה של אותו נר אצלו. השבירה מתה כש-1 וגם 2 חצו אותו; נכס 3 נמדד ומוצג אבל לא מכריע. בזוג: כש-3 וגם 4 חצו.\nכבוי: מספיק שנכס אחד חוצה כדי לבטל.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_qt_on    = input.bool(true, title="Quarterly Theory — מיכלים ורבע ראשון",
     tooltip="שבירה מתה כשהמיכל שלה נגמר, גם אם לא נלקחה — 1m: מיקרו 90 דק׳, 5m: סשן, 15m: יום מסחר, 1H: שבוע, 4H: חודש (שבוע 5 ושבוע מת: מיכל לעצמם), יומי: רבעון QT, שבועי: שנת QT, חודשי: מחזור 4 שנים.\nPSP שנולד ברבע הראשון של המיכל או בזמן חסום — לפי ההגדרה שמתחת.\nשעון ניו יורק, היום מתחיל ב-18:00.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_q1_mode  = input.string("בצבע נפרד", title="PSP ברבע ראשון / זמן חסום",
     options=["בצבע נפרד", "רגיל", "לא קיים"],
     tooltip="PSP שנולד ברבע הראשון של המיכל שלו, או בזמן חסום (שישי ב-1H; שישי של שבוע 4, שבוע 5 ושבוע מת ב-4H).\n• בצבע נפרד = PSP מלא בכל מקום — סימון, שורה, תיבה, התראה ו-Hub — בצבע 'רבע ראשון / זמן חסום'.\n• רגיל = PSP מלא בכל מקום, בצבע הרגיל שלו.\n• לא קיים = לא נכנס לשום מקום: לא סימון, לא שורה, לא תיבה, לא התראה ולא Hub. שבירה ישנה יותר שמתחתיו נשארת מוצגת.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_inv_wick = input.bool(true, title="בטל שבירה לפי פתיל",
     tooltip="דלוק (ברירת מחדל): מספיק שפתיל חוצה את רמת הסווינג כדי שהשבירה תפסיק להיחשב.\nכבוי: רק נר שנסגר מעבר לרמה מבטל.",
     group=grp_mtf)
i_col_neut = input.color(color.new(#ffffff, 15), title="צבע הכותרת ADI", group=grp_mtf)
i_mtf_alert = input.bool(true, title="התראה על שבירה חדשה", group=grp_mtf)
i_long_tf  = input.bool(false, title="סרוק גם 1D ו-1W (בגרף מתחת ליומי)",
     tooltip="כבוי (ברירת מחדל): חוסך סדרות נתונים — התקציב משותף לכל האינדיקטורים בגרף, ו-Bar Replay חרג ממנו. המרכז צריך רק עד 4H.\nבגרף יומי ומעלה הם נסרקים תמיד.",
     group=grp_mtf)

grp_fast   = "═══  התרעה מהירה 5m / 15m  ═══"
i_fast_on  = input.bool(true, title="הצג התרעת 5m / 15m",
     tooltip="תיבה נפרדת משלה. נעלמת מעצמה בסגירת הנר הבא של אותה מסגרת.\nשורה בצבע הזוג = PSP של 3–4.",
     group=grp_fast)
i_fast_pcp = input.bool(true, title="כלול גם PCP (דיברגנס בלי סווינג)",
     tooltip="PSP מוצג בצבע עם ⚡, והשמות לידו הם הנכסים שעוד לא חצו את הקצה של נר הסווינג. PSP שאף אחד כבר לא מחזיק לא מוצג.\nPCP מוצג עם ◦, נר אחד מוקדם יותר כי הוא לא מחכה לסווינג. הוא נעלם ברגע שהנר כבר לא יכול להיות סווינג.",
     group=grp_fast)
i_fast_v   = input.string("למעלה", title="גובה ההתרעה",
     options=["למעלה", "באמצע", "למטה"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_h   = input.string("ימין", title="צד ההתרעה",
     options=["שמאל", "מרכז", "ימין"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_pad = input.int(0, title="הרחקת ההתרעה מהקצה (שורות)", minval=0, maxval=12, group=grp_fast)
i_fast_sz  = input.string("גדול", title="גודל הטקסט",
     options=["קטן", "רגיל", "גדול", "ענק"], group=grp_fast)
i_fast_bg  = input.bool(true, title="רקע מודגש", group=grp_fast)
i_fast_idle = input.bool(true, title="החזק את התיבה גם כשאין אות",
     tooltip="מציג \"15m —\" ו-\"5m —\" כשאין כלום, כדי שאפשר יהיה לראות שהתיבה חיה ואיפה היא יושבת.",
     group=grp_fast)
i_fast_alert = input.bool(true, title="התראה (alert) על PSP מהיר",
     tooltip="שולח alert כשנוצר PSP מהיר. לכל היותר אחת לנר של הגרף.",
     group=grp_fast)

// Q1 / blocked: coloured, ordinary, or not there at all.
q1Col  = i_q1_mode == "בצבע נפרד"
q1Drop = i_q1_mode == "לא קיים"

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  TIMEFRAME GATE  (chart drawing only — the corner line is independent)
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

tf_str = timeframe.period

is_1m  = tf_str == "1"
is_5m  = tf_str == "5"
is_15m = tf_str == "15"
is_1h  = tf_str == "60"
is_4h  = tf_str == "240"
is_1d  = tf_str == "D"
is_1w  = tf_str == "W"
is_1mo = timeframe.ismonthly and timeframe.multiplier == 1

// Which Quarterly Theory ladder the chart's own bars sit on. 0 = none, and a
// timeframe with no ladder simply never expires and is never coloured.
chKind = is_1m ? 1 : is_5m ? 2 : is_15m ? 3 : is_1h ? 4 : is_4h ? 5 : is_1d ? 6 : is_1w ? 7 : is_1mo ? 8 : 0

// chartSec lives here rather than down beside the line, because the weakness
// rule needs it before the detection below.
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)

// Weakness is a DAILY-and-above rule. On the chart's own bars that means the
// chart itself has to be 1D or higher; the stepped 1D/1W engines carry it
// whatever chart you are standing on.
ymwTfOk = i_ym_weak and chartSec >= timeframe.in_seconds("D")

tf_allowed = (is_1m  and i_tf_1m)  or
             (is_5m  and i_tf_5m)  or
             (is_15m and i_tf_15m) or
             (is_1h  and i_tf_1h)  or
             (is_4h  and i_tf_4h)  or
             (is_1d  and i_tf_1d)  or
             (is_1w  and i_tf_1w)  or
             (is_1mo and i_tf_1mo)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CANDLE DIRECTION  (+1 Bull / -1 Bear / 0 Doji)
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_dir(float o, float c) =>
    c > o ? 1 : c < o ? -1 : 0

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ASSETS AND CHART-TIMEFRAME FETCHES
//  lookahead_off → proper backtest support for all timeframes
//  gaps_off      → no na bars when the external symbol has no tick
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// The label for a symbol: no exchange, no continuous-contract suffix, and the
// micro roots read as the instrument they track.
f_nm(string s) =>
    parts = str.split(s, ":")
    r = str.replace_all(str.replace_all(array.get(parts, array.size(parts) - 1), "1!", ""), "2!", "")
    r == "MNQ" ? "NQ" : r == "MES" ? "ES" : r == "MYM" ? "YM" : r == "M2K" ? "RTY" : r == "MGC" ? "GC" : r

nmN = f_nm(i_sym1)
nmE = f_nm(i_sym2)
nmY = f_nm(i_sym3)
nmR = f_nm(i_sym4)

// Asset 4 switched off asks for exactly what asset 3 asks for, so the
// requests are shared and cost nothing. The pair needs both 3 and 4.
usePair = i_use4 and i_use_ym
sym4    = i_use4 ? i_sym4 : i_sym3

settleMode = i_settle == "דלוק" ? settlement_as_close.on : i_settle == "ברירת המחדל של הסימבול" ? settlement_as_close.inherit : settlement_as_close.off
adjMode    = i_adjust == "מיושר לגלגול" ? backadjustment.on : i_adjust == "בלי יישור" ? backadjustment.off : backadjustment.inherit

tk_nq = ticker.modify(i_sym1, backadjustment = adjMode, settlement_as_close = settleMode)
tk_es = ticker.modify(i_sym2, backadjustment = adjMode, settlement_as_close = settleMode)
tk_ym = ticker.modify(i_sym3, backadjustment = adjMode, settlement_as_close = settleMode)
tk_rt = ticker.modify(sym4,   backadjustment = adjMode, settlement_as_close = settleMode)

f_sec(simple string sym) =>
    [o, h, l, c] = request.security(sym, timeframe.period,
         [open, high, low, close],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    [o, h, l, c]

[a_nq_o, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, a_nq_c] = f_sec(tk_nq)
[a_es_o, a_es_h, a_es_l, a_es_c] = f_sec(tk_es)
[a_ym_o, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, a_ym_c] = f_sec(tk_ym)
[a_rt_o, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, a_rt_c] = f_sec(tk_rt)

nq_dir = f_dir(a_nq_o, a_nq_c)
es_dir = f_dir(a_es_o, a_es_c)
ym_dir = f_dir(a_ym_o, a_ym_c)
rt_dir = f_dir(a_rt_o, a_rt_c)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PCP DETECTION
//
//  1 vs 2   : any direction mismatch is a divergence.
//  3 up     : STRENGTH — 3 closes UP while 1 and/or 2 close DOWN.
//  3 down   : WEAKNESS — 3 closes DOWN while the others close UP. Daily and
//             above only, and only when neither rule above already fired.
//  3 vs 4   : the pair — they close in opposite directions. Its own category.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

nq_ok = i_use_nq and (not i_ignore_doji or nq_dir != 0)
es_ok = i_use_es and (not i_ignore_doji or es_dir != 0)
ym_ok = i_use_ym and (not i_ignore_doji or ym_dir != 0)
rt_ok = usePair  and (not i_ignore_doji or rt_dir != 0)

div_es_nq = nq_ok and es_ok and (nq_dir != es_dir)

div_ym = ym_ok and ym_dir > 0 and
         ((es_ok and es_dir < 0) or (nq_ok and nq_dir < 0))

div_ymw = ymwTfOk and ym_ok and ym_dir < 0 and
          ((es_ok and es_dir > 0) or (nq_ok and nq_dir > 0)) and
          not div_es_nq and not div_ym

is_pcp = div_es_nq or div_ym or div_ymw

div_pair = usePair and ym_ok and rt_ok and ym_dir != rt_dir

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PSP DETECTION  — 3-Bar Swing, Zero Repaint, No Flicker
//
//  Timeline:   bar[2] ←  bar[1]  ← bar[0]
//                       (SWING)    (confirms, current CLOSED bar)
//
//  The swing is checked on EVERY included asset, not only on the chart
//  symbol, so a swing on another asset is still marked — just faded.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

f_sw_hi(float h) => h[1] > h[2] and h[1] > h[0]
f_sw_lo(float l) => l[1] < l[2] and l[1] < l[0]

own_hi = f_sw_hi(high)
own_lo = f_sw_lo(low)

ext_hi = (i_use_nq  and f_sw_hi(a_nq_h)) or
         (i_use_es  and f_sw_hi(a_es_h)) or
         ((div_ym[1] or div_ymw[1]) and f_sw_hi(a_ym_h))

ext_lo = (i_use_nq  and f_sw_lo(a_nq_l)) or
         (i_use_es  and f_sw_lo(a_es_l)) or
         ((div_ym[1] or div_ymw[1]) and f_sw_lo(a_ym_l))

confirmed = barstate.isconfirmed
pcp_at_1  = is_pcp[1]          // immutable — bar[1] is fully closed

psp_base     = tf_allowed and confirmed and pcp_at_1

// Which asset the chart is — recognised by name, so NQ1! and MNQ1! are the
// same instrument. Both the ticker and the root are tried.
chNm  = f_nm(syminfo.ticker)
chNm2 = f_nm(syminfo.root)
f_isCh(string nm) => nm == chNm or nm == chNm2

// The chart's own swing is the TRIAD's own only when the chart is an asset
// that takes part in this divergence: 1 or 2 when included, 3 only when 3 is
// the one that diverged — the same rule ext_hi / ext_lo apply to every asset.
// On RTY, or on a symbol outside the set, a triad PSP is always "ext".
chOwnTri = (f_isCh(nmN) and i_use_nq) or (f_isCh(nmE) and i_use_es) or (f_isCh(nmY) and (div_ym[1] or div_ymw[1]))

psp_bear_own = psp_base and chOwnTri and own_hi
psp_bear_ext = psp_base and ext_hi and not psp_bear_own
psp_bull_own = psp_base and chOwnTri and own_lo
psp_bull_ext = psp_base and ext_lo and not psp_bull_own

// The pair's swing has to be on 3 or 4. It counts as the chart's own only
// when the chart IS one of the two.
chIsPair = usePair and (f_isCh(nmY) or f_isCh(nmR))
pr_hi    = f_sw_hi(a_ym_h) or f_sw_hi(a_rt_h)
pr_lo    = f_sw_lo(a_ym_l) or f_sw_lo(a_rt_l)

pp_base     = tf_allowed and confirmed and div_pair[1]
pp_bear_own = pp_base and chIsPair and own_hi
pp_bear_ext = pp_base and pr_hi and not pp_bear_own
pp_bull_own = pp_base and chIsPair and own_lo
pp_bull_ext = pp_base and pr_lo and not pp_bull_own

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  MARKER COLOURS AND THE PENDING DOT
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// The HUE says which rule fired, the transparency says whether the swing was
// on the chart's own asset. The weakness colour comes off bar[1].
wk1 = div_ymw[1]

c_bear_own = wk1 ? i_col_weak : i_col_bear
c_bull_own = wk1 ? i_col_weak : i_col_bull
c_bear_ext = color.new(c_bear_own, i_ext_transp)
c_bull_ext = color.new(c_bull_own, i_ext_transp)
c_pair_ext = color.new(i_col_pair, i_ext_transp)

// ── Pending: self-clearing, because a bar is undecided exactly while
//    barstate.isconfirmed is false. Historical bars are always confirmed.
pending = tf_allowed and i_show_pending and not confirmed

// Can bar[1] still become a swing on this asset? It has to be above (below)
// bar[2], and the bar forming now must not have gone past it yet.
f_canSw(float h, float l) =>
    (h[1] > h[2] and h < h[1]) or (l[1] < l[2] and l > l[1])

// Every call on every bar, outside any condition, so its history stays whole.
csN = f_canSw(a_nq_h, a_nq_l)
csE = f_canSw(a_es_h, a_es_l)
csY = f_canSw(a_ym_h, a_ym_l)
pcp1Live = (i_use_nq and csN) or (i_use_es and csE) or ((div_ym[1] or div_ymw[1]) and csY)

plotchar(pending and is_pcp    ? 1 : na, title="PCP Pending — Live Bar",
     char="•", location=location.abovebar, color=i_col_pend, size=size.tiny)

plotchar(pending and is_pcp[1] and pcp1Live ? 1 : na, title="PCP Pending — Previous Bar",
     char="•", location=location.abovebar, color=i_col_pend,
     offset=-1, size=size.tiny)

barcolor(tf_allowed and i_show_pcp_bars and is_pcp ? i_col_pcp : na,
     title="PCP Bar Tint")

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  HIGHER TIMEFRAMES
//
//  request.security returns RAW NUMBERS only — never a UDT and never an
//  array. Returning an object would make TradingView keep a copy per chart
//  bar per timeframe and blow the memory limit ("Memory limits exceeded",
//  which compiles cleanly and simply fails to load).
//
//  Every history offset is taken INSIDE the expression, so it is evaluated
//  in that timeframe's own context and a bar only enters the calculation
//  once it has closed. Zero repaint.
//
//  Index map in the requested timeframe's context:
//      [1] = last CLOSED bar   confirms the swing of [2], carries the close
//                              used for the "level taken" test, and is itself
//                              the bar the pending state is read from
//      [2] = the SWING bar
//      [3] = the bar before it
//
//  The call count is fixed in the source (4 timeframes × 4 assets = 16, plus
//  4 for the chart timeframe and 11 fast readers) and never varies with the
//  chart. Asset 4 off makes its requests identical to asset 3's, so they are
//  shared.
//
//  Limitation worth knowing: the state is built by stepping through the chart's
//  own history, so a timeframe can only be tracked as far back as the chart
//  reaches.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// What a stepped timeframe needs, and nothing more. d1/d2 are directions
// already reduced inside the request; swH/swL are the three-bar swing already
// decided there. hi2/lo2 are the swing bar's extremes, which become the level
// to defend. tkH/tkL are the bar that just closed.
type AB
    float d1  = na
    float d2  = na
    bool  swH = false
    bool  swL = false
    float hi2 = na
    float lo2 = na
    float tkH = na
    float tkL = na
    float rnH = na    // the bar still FORMING, accumulated from chart bars
    float rnL = na
    bool  cH  = false // bar[1] is above bar[2] — it could still be a swing high
    bool  cL  = false // bar[1] is below bar[2] — it could still be a swing low

// The fast heads-up keeps no state. Six flags packed into ONE number — +2
// swing high, +1 swing low, +4 that high taken, +8 that low taken, +16 bar[1]
// can still be a swing high, +32 a swing low — because every element of every
// request is a full series held over the history.
type FB
    float d1 = na
    float d2 = na
    float sw = na

// Two candle directions in ONE number, for the same reason. Each direction is
// a digit 0–3 — 0 down, 1 doji, 2 up, 3 no data — and the pair is d1*4 + d2.
f_dc(float o, float c) =>
    c > o ? 2.0 : c < o ? 0.0 : na(c) ? 3.0 : 1.0

f_ud(float q) =>
    na(q) or q == 3 ? na : q - 1.0

//  The clock rides INSIDE the tuple, as time[2] — the SWING candle's own
//  open. It moves exactly when a new bar opens, and it is also the birth time
//  the break's Quarterly Theory container is read from.
f_load(AB b, simple string sym, simple string tf) =>
    [tc, dd, sw, hi2, lo2, tkH, tkL] = request.security(sym, tf,
         [time[2],
          f_dc(open[1], close[1]) * 4 + f_dc(open[2], close[2]),
          (high[2] > high[3] and high[2] > high[1] ? 2.0 : 0.0) + (low[2] < low[3] and low[2] < low[1] ? 1.0 : 0.0) + (high[1] > high[2] ? 4.0 : 0.0) + (low[1] < low[2] ? 8.0 : 0.0),
          high[2], low[2],
          i_inv_wick ? high[1] : close[1],
          i_inv_wick ? low[1]  : close[1]],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    b.d1  := na(dd) ? na : f_ud(math.floor(dd / 4))
    b.d2  := na(dd) ? na : f_ud(dd % 4)
    b.swH := not na(sw) and sw % 4 >= 2
    b.swL := not na(sw) and sw % 2 == 1
    b.cH  := not na(sw) and sw % 8 >= 4
    b.cL  := not na(sw) and sw >= 8
    b.hi2 := hi2
    b.lo2 := lo2
    b.tkH := tkH
    b.tkL := tkL
    tc

f_fast(FB b, simple string sym, simple string tf) =>
    [dd, sw] = request.security(sym, tf,
         [f_dc(open[1], close[1]) * 4 + f_dc(open[2], close[2]),
          (high[2] > high[3] and high[2] > high[1] ? 2.0 : 0.0) + (low[2] < low[3] and low[2] < low[1] ? 1.0 : 0.0) + (math.max(i_inv_wick ? high[1] : close[1], i_inv_wick ? high : close) > high[2] ? 4.0 : 0.0) + (math.min(i_inv_wick ? low[1] : close[1], i_inv_wick ? low : close) < low[2] ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (high[1] > high[2] and high < high[1] ? 16.0 : 0.0) + (low[1] < low[2] and low > low[1] ? 32.0 : 0.0)],
         lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
         gaps      = barmerge.gaps_off)
    b.d1 := na(dd) ? na : f_ud(math.floor(dd / 4))
    b.d2 := na(dd) ? na : f_ud(dd % 4)
    b.sw := sw
    b.d2

// The high and low of the bar still forming on that timeframe, built up from
// the chart's own bars. rst is that timeframe's clock rolling.
f_run(AB b, float h, float l, bool rst) =>
    if not na(h) and not na(l)
        if rst or na(b.rnH)
            b.rnH := h
            b.rnL := l
        else
            b.rnH := math.max(b.rnH, h)
            b.rnL := math.min(b.rnL, l)
    b.rnH

// The chart's own timeframe needs no request — its series are already here.
f_fill(AB b, float o, float h, float l, float c) =>
    b.d1  := c[1] > o[1] ? 1.0 : c[1] < o[1] ? -1.0 : na(c[1]) ? na : 0.0
    b.d2  := c[2] > o[2] ? 1.0 : c[2] < o[2] ? -1.0 : na(c[2]) ? na : 0.0
    b.swH := h[2] > h[3] and h[2] > h[1]
    b.swL := l[2] < l[3] and l[2] < l[1]
    b.cH  := h[1] > h[2]
    b.cL  := l[1] < l[2]
    b.hi2 := h[2]
    b.lo2 := l[2]
    b.tkH := i_inv_wick ? h[1] : c[1]
    b.tkL := i_inv_wick ? l[1] : c[1]
    b.tkL

// One reusable object per asset per timeframe — allocated once, updated in
// place, so nothing accumulates across bars.
var AB n1h = AB.new()
var AB e1h = AB.new()
var AB y1h = AB.new()
var AB z1h = AB.new()
var AB n4h = AB.new()
var AB e4h = AB.new()
var AB y4h = AB.new()
var AB z4h = AB.new()
var AB n1d = AB.new()
var AB e1d = AB.new()
var AB y1d = AB.new()
var AB z1d = AB.new()
var AB n1w = AB.new()
var AB e1w = AB.new()
var AB y1w = AB.new()
var AB z1w = AB.new()
var AB nCh = AB.new()
var AB eCh = AB.new()
var AB yCh = AB.new()
var AB zCh = AB.new()
var FB n15 = FB.new()
var FB e15 = FB.new()
var FB y15 = FB.new()
var FB z15 = FB.new()
var FB n5m = FB.new()
var FB e5m = FB.new()
var FB y5m = FB.new()
var FB z5m = FB.new()
// 1m — only for the hub's SFP on a 15m chart (Fill on 15m + PSP two
// timeframes below). Not shown in the box. Triad only.
var FB n1m = FB.new()
var FB e1m = FB.new()
var FB y1m = FB.new()

tn1h = f_load(n1h, tk_nq, "60")
te1h = f_load(e1h, tk_es, "60")
ty1h = f_load(y1h, tk_ym, "60")
f_load(z1h, tk_rt, "60")

tn4h = f_load(n4h, tk_nq, "240")
te4h = f_load(e4h, tk_es, "240")
ty4h = f_load(y4h, tk_ym, "240")
f_load(z4h, tk_rt, "240")

// Off = the chart's own timeframe, so the 1D/1W engines are not stepped and
// not shown below a daily chart.
useLong = i_long_tf or chartSec >= timeframe.in_seconds("D")
tfD = useLong ? "D" : timeframe.period
tfW = useLong ? "W" : timeframe.period

tn1d = f_load(n1d, tk_nq, tfD)
te1d = f_load(e1d, tk_es, tfD)
ty1d = f_load(y1d, tk_ym, tfD)
f_load(z1d, tk_rt, tfD)

tn1w = f_load(n1w, tk_nq, tfW)
te1w = f_load(e1w, tk_es, tfW)
ty1w = f_load(y1w, tk_ym, tfW)
f_load(z1w, tk_rt, tfW)

// The fast timeframes. Read on the last bar only, never stepped through
// history, so a chart above them is not a problem.
f_fast(n15, tk_nq, "15")
f_fast(e15, tk_es, "15")
f_fast(y15, tk_ym, "15")
f_fast(z15, tk_rt, "15")

f_fast(n5m, tk_nq, "5")
f_fast(e5m, tk_es, "5")
f_fast(y5m, tk_ym, "5")
f_fast(z5m, tk_rt, "5")

f_fast(n1m, tk_nq, "1")
f_fast(e1m, tk_es, "1")
f_fast(y1m, tk_ym, "1")

f_fill(nCh, a_nq_o, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, a_nq_c)
f_fill(eCh, a_es_o, a_es_h, a_es_l, a_es_c)
f_fill(yCh, a_ym_o, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, a_ym_c)
f_fill(zCh, a_rt_o, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, a_rt_c)

// The clock each engine steps on, taken from whichever asset is enabled.
t1h = i_use_nq ? tn1h : i_use_es ? te1h : ty1h
t4h = i_use_nq ? tn4h : i_use_es ? te4h : ty4h
t1d = i_use_nq ? tn1d : i_use_es ? te1d : ty1d
t1w = i_use_nq ? tn1w : i_use_es ? te1w : ty1w
t2  = time[2]

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PER-TIMEFRAME STATE
//  Lives in var on the CHART's timeline, which is where state belongs.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

type MtfSt
    int    lastT  = 0     // time of the bar already stepped — blocks a double step
    bool   live   = false // a break is standing right now
    int    dir    = 0     // -1 bearish · 1 bullish
    string who    = ""    // who is still defending it, or "ALL"
    bool   isNew  = false // set on the chart bar the break was recorded
    bool   weak   = false // the break came from the weakness rule
    bool   q1     = false // born in the first quarter or a blocked time
    bool   pair   = false // a 3–4 break
    bool   pndOn  = false // the bar that just closed is a PCP, verdict not in
    string pndWho = ""
    float  phN    = na    // that candle's high / low on each asset, kept only
    float  plN    = na    // while it can still be a swing there
    float  phE    = na
    float  plE    = na
    float  phY    = na
    float  plY    = na

// Has the level been taken? tkH and tkL are already the right side to compare.
f_taken(float lvl, int dir, float tkH, float tkL) =>
    na(lvl) ? false : dir == -1 ? tkH > lvl : tkL < lvl

// Who took part in the divergence — for the pending state and the fast PCP.
f_who(bool divP, bool divY, bool divW, bool okN, bool okE, int dn, int de) =>
    pN = divP or (divY and okN and dn < 0) or (divW and okN and dn > 0)
    pE = divP or (divY and okE and de < 0) or (divW and okE and de > 0)
    ym = divY or divW
    w  = pN and pE and ym ? "ALL" : ""
    if w == ""
        if pN
            w := nmN
        if pE
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + nmE
        if ym
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + nmY
    w

// One stored break: the direction, how many of the two deciders were tracked,
// and the level each asset defends — the SWING CANDLE's own extreme on that
// asset's chart. In a pair break, nq holds asset 3's level and es asset 4's,
// so the same erase-and-decide code serves both.
type Brk
    int    dir  = 0
    int    core = 0
    bool   weak = false
    float  nq   = na
    float  es   = na
    float  ym   = na
    int    cont = na     // the Quarterly Theory container it was born in
    int    born = na     // the swing candle's open
    bool   q1   = false  // born in the first quarter or a blocked time
    bool   pair = false  // a 3–4 break

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  QUARTERLY THEORY
//
//  Each timeframe compares the four quarters of a larger cycle, its
//  container. f_cyc reads a timestamp and returns which container it falls in
//  — an id that only has to be equal for two times in the same container — and
//  whether it is the first quarter of that container or a blocked time.
//
//      kind  chart  quarters          container        first quarter / blocked
//      1     1m     22.5 min          90-min micro     first 22.5 min
//      2     5m     90-min micro      6-hour session   first 90 min
//      3     15m    6-hour session    trading day      Asia
//      4     1H     day               week             Monday · Friday
//      5     4H     week (by Tue)     month            week 1 · week-4 Friday ·
//                                                      week 5 · dead week
//      6     1D     quarter/4         QT quarter       first quarter/4
//      7     1W     QT quarter        QT year (Apr)    April–June
//      8     1Mo    calendar year     4-year cycle     year 1 (2023, 2027…)
//
//  Week 5 and a dead week are each a container of their own — they belong to
//  neither the month before nor the month after.
//  What happens to such a PSP is the i_q1_mode setting.
//
//  The trading day opens at 18:00 New York. Shifting every time by six hours
//  turns that into midnight, so the calendar functions read the trading day
//  directly. DST changes on a Sunday morning, outside the trading week, so
//  stepping in whole days between Monday and Friday is exact.
//  Sunday 18:00 shifts to Monday, so for futures Sunday never appears; on a
//  24/7 market a Sunday trading day belongs to the week BEFORE it, as in the
//  SSMT and Fill indicators.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

NY     = "America/New_York"
DAY_MS = 86400000

f_cyc(int t, int k) =>
    int  cont = na
    bool q1   = false
    if not na(t) and k > 0
        td   = t + 21600000
        y    = year(td, NY)
        m    = month(td, NY)
        w    = dayofweek(td, NY)
        hh   = hour(td, NY)
        mod  = hh * 60 + minute(td, NY)
        d0   = timestamp(NY, y, m, dayofmonth(td, NY), 0, 0)
        dsm  = w == dayofweek.sunday ? 6 : w - 2
        mon  = d0 - dsm * DAY_MS
        tue  = mon + DAY_MS
        thu  = mon + 3 * DAY_MS
        fri  = w == dayofweek.friday
        // a week belongs to the month of its Tuesday; numbered by its Tuesday
        dead = month(tue, NY) != month(thu, NY)
        wkN  = dead ? 0 : math.floor((dayofmonth(tue, NY) - 1) / 7) + 1
        if k == 1
            cont := d0 + math.floor(mod / 90)
            q1   := (mod % 90) * 2 < 45
        else if k == 2
            s6   = math.floor(hh / 6)
            cont := d0 + s6
            q1   := mod - s6 * 360 < 90
        else if k == 3
            cont := d0
            q1   := hh < 6
        else if k == 4
            cont := mon
            q1   := w == dayofweek.monday or fri
        else if k == 5
            // week 5 and a dead week are a container of their own (a Monday
            // timestamp — it can never collide with year*12+month)
            own  = dead or wkN == 5
            cont := own ? mon : year(tue, NY) * 12 + month(tue, NY)
            q1   := own or wkN == 1 or (wkN == 4 and fri)
        else if k == 6
            // the real quarter cut into four equal parts, so the last boundary
            // lands exactly on the quarter's last day
            qm = math.floor((m - 1) / 3)
            qs = timestamp(NY, y, qm * 3 + 1, 1, 0, 0)
            qe = qm == 3 ? timestamp(NY, y + 1, 1, 1, 0, 0) : timestamp(NY, y, qm * 3 + 4, 1, 0, 0)
            di = math.round((d0 - qs) / DAY_MS)
            ql = math.round((qe - qs) / DAY_MS)
            cont := y * 4 + qm
            q1   := math.floor(di * 4 / ql) == 0
        else if k == 7
            // QT year opens in April; Q1 is April–June
            tm = month(tue, NY)
            ty = year(tue, NY)
            cont := tm >= 4 ? ty : ty - 1
            q1   := tm >= 4 and tm <= 6
        else if k == 8
            // calendar 4-year cycle from 2023
            cont := math.floor((y - 2023) / 4)
            q1   := (y - 2023) % 4 == 0
    [cont, q1]

// Who is STILL defending this break — read off the levels that have not been
// erased. A triad break always names 1 or 2; a pair break never does.
f_holds(Brk b) =>
    w = b.pair ? "" : ""
    if b.pair
        if not na(b.nq)
            w := nmY
        if not na(b.es)
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + nmR
    else
        if not na(b.nq)
            w := nmN
        if not na(b.es)
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + nmE
        if not na(b.ym)
            w := w + (w == "" ? "" : " ") + nmY
        if not na(b.nq) and not na(b.es) and not na(b.ym)
            w := "ALL"
    w

// Does this bar finish the break off? A level that gets taken is ERASED, which
// is what lets the levels be taken on different bars and still add up.
// The two deciders — 1 and 2, or 3 and 4 in a pair — end it once both are
// gone. A decider switched off never held a level and does not vote.
f_kill(Brk b, float nH, float nL, float eH, float eL, float yH, float yL, bool major) =>
    hit = false
    if not na(b.nq) and f_taken(b.nq, b.dir, nH, nL)
        b.nq := na
        hit := true
    if not na(b.es) and f_taken(b.es, b.dir, eH, eL)
        b.es := na
        hit := true
    if not na(b.ym) and f_taken(b.ym, b.dir, yH, yL)
        b.ym := na
        hit := true
    coreGone = na(b.nq) and na(b.es)
    major ? (b.core > 0 ? coreGone : na(b.ym)) : hit

// What is on display: the newest survivor, or nothing.
f_show(MtfSt s, array<Brk> st) =>
    s.live := array.size(st) > 0
    if s.live
        top = array.get(st, 0)
        s.dir  := top.dir
        s.who  := f_holds(top)
        s.weak := top.weak
        s.q1   := top.q1
        s.pair := top.pair
    s.live

// One step per closed bar of that timeframe. Invalidation is checked before
// detection, so a level taken and a fresh swing on the same bar resolve in
// the right order.
f_step(MtfSt s, array<Brk> st, int t, AB n, AB e, AB y, bool allowW, int kind, int cNow) =>
    s.isNew := false
    if not na(t) and t != s.lastT
        s.lastT := t

        // ── 1. let the closing bar take whatever levels it reaches
        i = 0
        while i < array.size(st)
            if f_kill(array.get(st, i), n.tkH, n.tkL, e.tkH, e.tkL, y.tkH, y.tkL, i_kill_all)
                array.remove(st, i)
            else
                i += 1

        // ── 2. the bar that just closed, [1]: a PCP whose swing verdict
        //       needs the NEXT close. Replaced wholesale on the next step.
        qN  = i_use_nq and not na(n.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d1 != 0)
        qE  = i_use_es and not na(e.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d1 != 0)
        qY  = i_use_ym and not na(y.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d1 != 0)
        qP  = qN and qE and n.d1 != e.d1
        qYm = qY and y.d1 > 0 and ((qE and e.d1 < 0) or (qN and n.d1 < 0))
        qYw = allowW and qY and y.d1 < 0 and ((qE and e.d1 > 0) or (qN and n.d1 > 0)) and not qP and not qYm
        s.pndOn  := qP or qYm or qYw
        s.pndWho := s.pndOn ? f_who(qP, qYm, qYw, qN, qE, int(n.d1), int(e.d1)) : ""
        // Only the sides where it could still be a swing are kept. tkH/tkL is
        // that candle's own high/low under the wick rule.
        pY = qYm or qYw
        s.phN := s.pndOn and i_use_nq and n.cH ? n.tkH : na
        s.plN := s.pndOn and i_use_nq and n.cL ? n.tkL : na
        s.phE := s.pndOn and i_use_es and e.cH ? e.tkH : na
        s.plE := s.pndOn and i_use_es and e.cL ? e.tkL : na
        s.phY := s.pndOn and pY and y.cH ? y.tkH : na
        s.plY := s.pndOn and pY and y.cL ? y.tkL : na

        // ── 3. a new PSP on the swing bar, [2] ──
        okN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d2 != 0)
        okE = i_use_es and not na(e.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d2 != 0)
        okY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)

        divP = okN and okE and n.d2 != e.d2
        divY = okY and y.d2 > 0 and ((okE and e.d2 < 0) or (okN and n.d2 < 0))
        divW = allowW and okY and y.d2 < 0 and ((okE and e.d2 > 0) or (okN and n.d2 > 0)) and not divP and not divY

        if divP or divY or divW
            ymIn = divY or divW
            hiN = i_use_nq and n.swH
            hiE = i_use_es and e.swH
            hiY = ymIn     and y.swH
            loN = i_use_nq and n.swL
            loE = i_use_es and e.swL
            loY = ymIn     and y.swL

            nHi = (hiN ? 1 : 0) + (hiE ? 1 : 0) + (hiY ? 1 : 0)
            nLo = (loN ? 1 : 0) + (loE ? 1 : 0) + (loY ? 1 : 0)

            // t is the swing candle's own open. One whose container already
            // ended by the time it was confirmed is dead on arrival. One born
            // in Q1 / a blocked time does not exist when the setting says so.
            [bc, bq] = f_cyc(t, kind)

            if (nHi > 0 or nLo > 0) and (na(cNow) or na(bc) or bc == cNow) and not (q1Drop and bq)
                bear = nHi >= nLo          // tie goes to the swing high
                array.unshift(st, Brk.new(bear ? -1 : 1,
                     (i_use_nq ? 1 : 0) + (i_use_es ? 1 : 0),
                     divW,
                     i_use_nq ? (bear ? n.hi2 : n.lo2) : na,
                     i_use_es ? (bear ? e.hi2 : e.lo2) : na,
                     i_use_ym ? (bear ? y.hi2 : y.lo2) : na,
                     bc, t, bq, false))
                while array.size(st) > i_depth
                    array.pop(st)
                s.isNew := true

        f_show(s, st)
    s.live

// The 3–4 pair, stepped the same way. 3 and 4 are equals: a break needs them
// to close in opposite directions on a candle that is a swing on either one,
// and it lives until both have crossed that candle's extreme.
f_stepP(MtfSt s, array<Brk> st, int t, AB y, AB r, int kind, int cNow) =>
    s.isNew := false
    if not na(t) and t != s.lastT
        s.lastT := t
        i = 0
        while i < array.size(st)
            if f_kill(array.get(st, i), y.tkH, y.tkL, r.tkH, r.tkL, na, na, i_kill_all)
                array.remove(st, i)
            else
                i += 1
        okY = not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)
        okR = not na(r.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or r.d2 != 0)
        if okY and okR and y.d2 != r.d2
            nHi = (y.swH ? 1 : 0) + (r.swH ? 1 : 0)
            nLo = (y.swL ? 1 : 0) + (r.swL ? 1 : 0)
            [bc, bq] = f_cyc(t, kind)
            if (nHi > 0 or nLo > 0) and (na(cNow) or na(bc) or bc == cNow) and not (q1Drop and bq)
                bear = nHi >= nLo
                array.unshift(st, Brk.new(bear ? -1 : 1, 2, false,
                     bear ? y.hi2 : y.lo2,
                     bear ? r.hi2 : r.lo2,
                     na, bc, t, bq, true))
                while array.size(st) > i_depth
                    array.pop(st)
                s.isNew := true
        f_show(s, st)
    s.live

// Run EVERY chart bar: a pending PCP dies once no asset can make it a swing —
// the forming candle went past its high on every asset that could still make
// a swing high, and past its low on every one that could make a swing low.
f_pnd(MtfSt s, AB n, AB e, AB y) =>
    if s.pndOn
        if i_inv_wick
            if not na(s.phN) and n.rnH >= s.phN
                s.phN := na
            if not na(s.plN) and n.rnL <= s.plN
                s.plN := na
            if not na(s.phE) and e.rnH >= s.phE
                s.phE := na
            if not na(s.plE) and e.rnL <= s.plE
                s.plE := na
            if not na(s.phY) and y.rnH >= s.phY
                s.phY := na
            if not na(s.plY) and y.rnL <= s.plY
                s.plY := na
        s.pndOn := not na(s.phN) or not na(s.plN) or not na(s.phE) or not na(s.plE) or not na(s.phY) or not na(s.plY)
    s.pndOn

// Run EVERY chart bar: this is what notices a level being taken by a candle
// that has not closed, and a container that rolled under a break that was
// never touched. It only shortens a break's life, never creates one.
// For a pair, a = asset 3 and b = asset 4; c is ignored (no third level).
f_cut(MtfSt s, array<Brk> st, AB a, AB b, AB c, int cNow) =>
    if array.size(st) > 0
        i = 0
        while i < array.size(st)
            k    = array.get(st, i)
            expd = not na(cNow) and not na(k.cont) and k.cont != cNow
            took = i_inv_wick and f_kill(k, a.rnH, a.rnL, b.rnH, b.rnL, c.rnH, c.rnL, i_kill_all)
            if expd or took
                array.remove(st, i)
            else
                i += 1
        f_show(s, st)
    s.live

var MtfSt st1h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st4h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st1d = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt st1w = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt stCh = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt ps1h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt ps4h = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt ps1d = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt ps1w = MtfSt.new()
var MtfSt psCh = MtfSt.new()

// One stack per timeframe, newest break first — the triad's and the pair's.
var array<Brk> b1h = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> b4h = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> b1d = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> b1w = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> bCh = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> p1h = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> p4h = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> p1d = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> p1w = array.new<Brk>()
var array<Brk> pCh = array.new<Brk>()

// The clock rolls exactly when the previous bar of that timeframe closed, so
// comparing it with the state's lastT — BEFORE f_step consumes it — is what
// says "a new bar started here, begin the accumulator again".
rs1h = t1h != st1h.lastT
rs4h = t4h != st4h.lastT
rs1d = t1d != st1d.lastT
rs1w = t1w != st1w.lastT

f_run(n1h, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, rs1h)
f_run(e1h, a_es_h, a_es_l, rs1h)
f_run(y1h, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, rs1h)
f_run(z1h, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, rs1h)
f_run(n4h, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, rs4h)
f_run(e4h, a_es_h, a_es_l, rs4h)
f_run(y4h, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, rs4h)
f_run(z4h, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, rs4h)
f_run(n1d, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, rs1d)
f_run(e1d, a_es_h, a_es_l, rs1d)
f_run(y1d, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, rs1d)
f_run(z1d, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, rs1d)
f_run(n1w, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, rs1w)
f_run(e1w, a_es_h, a_es_l, rs1w)
f_run(y1w, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, rs1w)
f_run(z1w, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, rs1w)
f_run(nCh, a_nq_h, a_nq_l, true)
f_run(eCh, a_es_h, a_es_l, true)
f_run(yCh, a_ym_h, a_ym_l, true)
f_run(zCh, a_rt_h, a_rt_l, true)

// The container each engine is in RIGHT NOW, read off the chart bar's own
// time. A break whose container differs has run out of time.
qkCh = i_qt_on ? chKind : 0
qk1h = i_qt_on ? 4 : 0
qk4h = i_qt_on ? 5 : 0
qk1d = i_qt_on ? 6 : 0
qk1w = i_qt_on ? 7 : 0

[cNowCh, xNowCh] = f_cyc(time, qkCh)
[cNow1h, xNow1h] = f_cyc(time, qk1h)
[cNow4h, xNow4h] = f_cyc(time, qk4h)
[cNow1d, xNow1d] = f_cyc(time, qk1d)
[cNow1w, xNow1w] = f_cyc(time, qk1w)

// 1H and 4H never get the weakness rule; 1D and 1W always do; the chart's own
// timeframe only when the chart itself is daily or higher.
f_step(stCh, bCh, t2, nCh, eCh, yCh, ymwTfOk, qkCh, cNowCh)
f_step(st1h, b1h, t1h, n1h, e1h, y1h, false, qk1h, cNow1h)
f_step(st4h, b4h, t4h, n4h, e4h, y4h, false, qk4h, cNow4h)
if useLong
    f_step(st1d, b1d, t1d, n1d, e1d, y1d, i_ym_weak, qk1d, cNow1d)
    f_step(st1w, b1w, t1w, n1w, e1w, y1w, i_ym_weak, qk1w, cNow1w)
if usePair
    f_stepP(psCh, pCh, t2, yCh, zCh, qkCh, cNowCh)
    f_stepP(ps1h, p1h, t1h, y1h, z1h, qk1h, cNow1h)
    f_stepP(ps4h, p4h, t4h, y4h, z4h, qk4h, cNow4h)
    if useLong
        f_stepP(ps1d, p1d, t1d, y1d, z1d, qk1d, cNow1d)
        f_stepP(ps1w, p1w, t1w, y1w, z1w, qk1w, cNow1w)

// …and then let the unfinished bar take whatever it has already reached, and
// the clock retire whatever has run out of container.
f_pnd(stCh, nCh, eCh, yCh)
f_pnd(st1h, n1h, e1h, y1h)
f_pnd(st4h, n4h, e4h, y4h)
if useLong
    f_pnd(st1d, n1d, e1d, y1d)
    f_pnd(st1w, n1w, e1w, y1w)

f_cut(stCh, bCh, nCh, eCh, yCh, cNowCh)
f_cut(st1h, b1h, n1h, e1h, y1h, cNow1h)
f_cut(st4h, b4h, n4h, e4h, y4h, cNow4h)
if useLong
    f_cut(st1d, b1d, n1d, e1d, y1d, cNow1d)
    f_cut(st1w, b1w, n1w, e1w, y1w, cNow1w)
if usePair
    f_cut(psCh, pCh, yCh, zCh, yCh, cNowCh)
    f_cut(ps1h, p1h, y1h, z1h, y1h, cNow1h)
    f_cut(ps4h, p4h, y4h, z4h, y4h, cNow4h)
    if useLong
        f_cut(ps1d, p1d, y1d, z1d, y1d, cNow1d)
        f_cut(ps1w, p1w, y1w, z1w, y1w, cNow1w)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE MARKERS ON THE CHART
//
//  Kept as DATA through history and drawn once, on the last bar: a marker has
//  to be erasable when its candle is taken, and drawing only at the end means
//  no label is ever created and destroyed on the way there.
//
//  Each marker carries a Brk — the swing candle's own extreme on each asset —
//  so it is judged by the same rule as the line and cannot drift from it.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

type Mk
    int    x
    float  y
    string tx
    color  col
    Brk    b
    float  own  = na   // that candle's extreme on THIS chart
    int    cont = na   // its Quarterly Theory container

var array<Mk> mks = array.new<Mk>()

// The swing candle is bar[1]. Its values are read here, at global scope, so
// the functions below never take a history offset themselves.
cH1 = high[1]
cL1 = low[1]
nH1 = a_nq_h[1]
nL1 = a_nq_l[1]
eH1 = a_es_h[1]
eL1 = a_es_l[1]
yH1 = a_ym_h[1]
yL1 = a_ym_l[1]
rH1 = a_rt_h[1]
rL1 = a_rt_l[1]
t1  = time[1]

// Every level keeps being erased as it falls, whichever rule is selected —
// only the verdict differs.
f_mdead(Mk m, int cNow) =>
    if m.b.pair
        f_kill(m.b, yCh.tkH, yCh.tkL, zCh.tkH, zCh.tkL, na, na, false)
        if i_inv_wick
            f_kill(m.b, yCh.rnH, yCh.rnL, zCh.rnH, zCh.rnL, na, na, false)
    else
        f_kill(m.b, nCh.tkH, nCh.tkL, eCh.tkH, eCh.tkL, yCh.tkH, yCh.tkL, false)
        if i_inv_wick
            f_kill(m.b, nCh.rnH, nCh.rnL, eCh.rnH, eCh.rnL, yCh.rnH, yCh.rnL, false)
    // The chart's own candle, straight off the chart's own series.
    if not na(m.own) and (f_taken(m.own, m.b.dir, cH1, cL1) or (i_inv_wick and f_taken(m.own, m.b.dir, high, low)))
        m.own := na
    rOwn = na(m.own)
    rCor = na(m.b.nq) and na(m.b.es)
    rAll = rCor and na(m.b.ym)
    expd = not na(cNow) and not na(m.cont) and m.cont != cNow
    expd or (i_mark_rule == "הנכס של הגרף" ? rOwn :
     i_mark_rule == "שני המכריעים" ? rCor :
     i_mark_rule == "כל הנכסים" ? rAll : rOwn)

// Prune BEFORE adding. tkH/tkL on the chart's own timeframe is bar[1], the
// swing bar a marker born on this bar sits on — testing a new marker against
// its own candle would kill it on birth.
if i_mark_erase and array.size(mks) > 0
    mi = 0
    while mi < array.size(mks)
        if f_mdead(array.get(mks, mi), cNowCh)
            array.remove(mks, mi)
        else
            mi += 1

// The gap in a unit that means the same everywhere: a fraction of ATR.
markGap = nz(ta.atr(14)) * i_mark_gap / 100.0

// One-line statements on purpose — see the note above mtfTop.
markSz = i_mark_sz == "זעיר" ? size.tiny : i_mark_sz == "קטן" ? size.small : i_mark_sz == "גדול" ? size.large : i_mark_sz == "ענק" ? size.huge : size.normal

// One shape for both. Where the swing happened is carried by the fade alone.
f_glyph(bool bear) =>
    i_mark_gl == "משולש גדול ▲" ? (bear ? "▲" : "▼") :
     i_mark_gl == "משולש קטן ▴" ? (bear ? "▴" : "▾") :
     i_mark_gl == "עיגול ●" ? "●" :
     i_mark_gl == "נקודה •" ? "•" :
     i_mark_gl == "ריבוע ■" ? "■" :
     i_mark_gl == "יהלום ◆" ? "◆" :
     i_mark_gl == "חץ ⬇" ? (bear ? "⬇" : "⬆") :
     i_mark_gl == "כוכב ★" ? "★" :
     i_mark_gl == "איקס ✕" ? "✕" :
     i_mark_gl == "טקסט משלי" ? (bear ? i_mark_tx_bear : i_mark_tx_bull) :
     (bear ? "▲" : "▼")

// The swing candle's container, and whether it is a first quarter or a
// blocked time — in which case the marker takes that colour instead, or does
// not exist at all, as the setting says.
[mkCont, mkQ1] = f_cyc(t1, qkCh)

f_mark(bool bear, bool own, color c, bool pair, float l1, float l2, float l3, int core) =>
    col = mkQ1 and q1Col ? color.new(i_col_q1, own ? 0 : i_ext_transp) : c
    array.unshift(mks, Mk.new(bar_index - 1, bear ? cH1 + markGap : cL1 - markGap, f_glyph(bear), col,
     Brk.new(bear ? -1 : 1, core, wk1 and not pair, l1, l2, l3, mkCont, t1, mkQ1, pair),
     bear ? cH1 : cL1, mkCont))
    // The window: Pine holds 500 label objects at most.
    while array.size(mks) > i_mark_keep
        array.pop(mks)
    array.size(mks)

core3 = (i_use_nq ? 1 : 0) + (i_use_es ? 1 : 0)

// A swing whose container already ended by the time it was confirmed is not
// kept at all — it would only be erased on the next bar. Neither is a Q1 /
// blocked one when the setting says it does not exist.
mkOk = bar_index > 2 and (na(cNowCh) or na(mkCont) or mkCont == cNowCh) and not (q1Drop and mkQ1)

if mkOk
    if psp_bear_own
        f_mark(true,  true,  c_bear_own, false, i_use_nq ? nH1 : na, i_use_es ? eH1 : na, i_use_ym ? yH1 : na, core3)
    if psp_bear_ext
        f_mark(true,  false, c_bear_ext, false, i_use_nq ? nH1 : na, i_use_es ? eH1 : na, i_use_ym ? yH1 : na, core3)
    if psp_bull_own
        f_mark(false, true,  c_bull_own, false, i_use_nq ? nL1 : na, i_use_es ? eL1 : na, i_use_ym ? yL1 : na, core3)
    if psp_bull_ext
        f_mark(false, false, c_bull_ext, false, i_use_nq ? nL1 : na, i_use_es ? eL1 : na, i_use_ym ? yL1 : na, core3)
    if pp_bear_own
        f_mark(true,  true,  i_col_pair, true, yH1, rH1, na, 2)
    if pp_bear_ext
        f_mark(true,  false, c_pair_ext, true, yH1, rH1, na, 2)
    if pp_bull_own
        f_mark(false, true,  i_col_pair, true, yL1, rL1, na, 2)
    if pp_bull_ext
        f_mark(false, false, c_pair_ext, true, yL1, rL1, na, 2)

// Drawn once, on the last bar: everything deleted, everything redrawn.
var array<label> mkDrawn = array.new<label>()
if barstate.islast
    while array.size(mkDrawn) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(mkDrawn))
    if array.size(mks) > 0
        for k = 0 to array.size(mks) - 1
            m = array.get(mks, k)
            array.push(mkDrawn, label.new(m.x, m.y, text = m.tx, style = label.style_none,
             yloc = yloc.price, textcolor = m.col, size = markSz))

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE LINE
//
//  Order:  1W · 1D · 4H · 1H · [your chart, only if it is 1H or higher]
//  Per timeframe: the triad's break, its ◦ if one is waiting, and the pair's
//  break in the pair colour. Cells pack left, so gaps close up.
//
//  A timeframe BELOW the chart's is left out: stepping it through history
//  would sample it once per chart bar, skipping whole bars of it. A timeframe
//  EQUAL to the chart's has no such problem — which is why these are >=.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

sh1h = timeframe.in_seconds("60")  >= chartSec
sh4h = timeframe.in_seconds("240") >= chartSec
sh1d = useLong and timeframe.in_seconds("D")   >= chartSec
sh1w = useLong and timeframe.in_seconds("W")   >= chartSec

// The chart's own timeframe joins the line only when it is 1H or higher AND
// not already one of the four above — 2H, 6H, 8H, 3D.
chDup   = is_1h or is_4h or is_1d or is_1w
chIsBig = chartSec >= timeframe.in_seconds("60") and not chDup

chName = is_1m ? "1m" : is_5m ? "5m" : is_15m ? "15m" : is_1h ? "1H" : is_4h ? "4H" : is_1d ? "1D" : is_1w ? "1W" : is_1mo ? "1Mo" : tf_str

f_arrow(MtfSt s) =>
    s.dir < 0 ? "▼" : "▲"

// The triad's cell: a standing break, or — with nothing standing — the ◦ of
// a bar that closed with a divergence and is waiting on its swing verdict.
f_rec(MtfSt s, string nm) =>
    s.live ? nm + " " + f_arrow(s) + " " + s.who : i_show_pending and s.pndOn ? nm + " ◦ " + s.pndWho : ""

// The pair's cell: a standing break only.
f_recP(MtfSt s, string nm) =>
    s.live ? nm + " " + f_arrow(s) + " " + s.who : ""

// A ◦ that needs its own cell: a break on display AND a new candle waiting.
f_dot(MtfSt s) =>
    i_show_pending and s.live and s.pndOn

// First quarter / blocked wins over every other colour — when it is coloured.
f_col(MtfSt s) =>
    s.live ? (s.q1 and q1Col ? i_col_q1 : s.pair ? i_col_pair : s.weak ? i_col_weak : s.dir < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull) : i_col_pend

r1w = sh1w ? f_rec(st1w, "1W") : ""
r1d = sh1d ? f_rec(st1d, "1D") : ""
r4h = sh4h ? f_rec(st4h, "4H") : ""
r1h = sh1h ? f_rec(st1h, "1H") : ""
rCh = tf_allowed and chIsBig ? f_rec(stCh, chName) : ""

rp1w = usePair and sh1w ? f_recP(ps1w, "1W") : ""
rp1d = usePair and sh1d ? f_recP(ps1d, "1D") : ""
rp4h = usePair and sh4h ? f_recP(ps4h, "4H") : ""
rp1h = usePair and sh1h ? f_recP(ps1h, "1H") : ""
rpCh = usePair and tf_allowed and chIsBig ? f_recP(psCh, chName) : ""

d1w = sh1w and f_dot(st1w)
d1d = sh1d and f_dot(st1d)
d4h = sh4h and f_dot(st4h)
d1h = sh1h and f_dot(st1h)
dCh = tf_allowed and chIsBig and f_dot(stCh)

// ── the fast heads-up ──
//  Deliberately NOT the carried-state engine. A PSP is a function of three
//  bars, so it can be read straight off the last bar, and that is what lets
//  this work on a timeframe below the chart's.
f_swH(float sw) =>
    not na(sw) and int(sw) % 4 >= 2

f_swL(float sw) =>
    not na(sw) and int(sw) % 2 == 1

// Still defending the swing candle's extreme: nothing since — neither the
// confirming bar nor the one still forming — has crossed it.
f_hold(float sw, int dir) =>
    not na(sw) and (dir < 0 ? int(sw) % 8 < 4 : int(sw) % 16 < 8)

// bar[1] can still become a swing on this asset — high side or low side.
f_canF(float sw) =>
    not na(sw) and int(sw) >= 16

f_flash(FB n, FB e, FB y) =>
    // ── PSP: the swing bar [2], confirmed by the bar that just closed ──
    okN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d2 != 0)
    okE = i_use_es and not na(e.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d2 != 0)
    okY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)

    divP = okN and okE and n.d2 != e.d2
    divY = okY and y.d2 > 0 and ((okE and e.d2 < 0) or (okN and n.d2 < 0))

    on  = false
    dir = 0
    who = ""
    if divP or divY
        hiN = i_use_nq and f_swH(n.sw)
        hiE = i_use_es and f_swH(e.sw)
        hiY = divY     and f_swH(y.sw)
        loN = i_use_nq and f_swL(n.sw)
        loE = i_use_es and f_swL(e.sw)
        loY = divY     and f_swL(y.sw)

        nHi = (hiN ? 1 : 0) + (hiE ? 1 : 0) + (hiY ? 1 : 0)
        nLo = (loN ? 1 : 0) + (loE ? 1 : 0) + (loY ? 1 : 0)

        if nHi > 0 or nLo > 0
            dir := nHi >= nLo ? -1 : 1
            // The line's rule: every enabled asset defends it, 1 and 2
            // decide, 3 never does.
            hN = i_use_nq and f_hold(n.sw, dir)
            hE = i_use_es and f_hold(e.sw, dir)
            hY = i_use_ym and f_hold(y.sw, dir)
            core = (i_use_nq ? 1 : 0) + (i_use_es ? 1 : 0)
            on  := i_kill_all ? (core > 0 ? (hN or hE) : hY) : ((not i_use_nq or hN) and (not i_use_es or hE) and (not i_use_ym or hY))
            who := hN and hE and hY ? "ALL" : (hN ? nmN : "") + (hE ? (hN ? " " : "") + nmE : "") + (hY ? (hN or hE ? " " : "") + nmY : "")

    // ── PCP: the bar that just closed, [1] — known one bar before the PSP.
    qN = i_use_nq and not na(n.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or n.d1 != 0)
    qE = i_use_es and not na(e.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or e.d1 != 0)
    qY = i_use_ym and not na(y.d1) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d1 != 0)

    qP  = qN and qE and n.d1 != e.d1
    qYm = qY and y.d1 > 0 and ((qE and e.d1 < 0) or (qN and n.d1 < 0))

    // …and only while some asset taking part can still make it a swing.
    pLive = (i_use_nq and f_canF(n.sw)) or (i_use_es and f_canF(e.sw)) or (qYm and f_canF(y.sw))
    pOn  = (qP or qYm) and pLive
    pWho = pOn ? f_who(qP, qYm, false, qN, qE, int(n.d1), int(e.d1)) : ""
    [on, dir, who, pOn, pWho]

// The pair on a fast timeframe: 3 and 4 in opposite directions on a swing.
f_flashP(FB y, FB r) =>
    on  = false
    dir = 0
    who = ""
    okY = usePair and not na(y.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or y.d2 != 0)
    okR = usePair and not na(r.d2) and (not i_ignore_doji or r.d2 != 0)
    if okY and okR and y.d2 != r.d2
        nHi = (f_swH(y.sw) ? 1 : 0) + (f_swH(r.sw) ? 1 : 0)
        nLo = (f_swL(y.sw) ? 1 : 0) + (f_swL(r.sw) ? 1 : 0)
        if nHi > 0 or nLo > 0
            dir := nHi >= nLo ? -1 : 1
            hY = f_hold(y.sw, dir)
            hR = f_hold(r.sw, dir)
            on  := i_kill_all ? (hY or hR) : (hY and hR)
            who := (hY ? nmY : "") + (hR ? (hY ? " " : "") + nmR : "")
    [on, dir, who]

[on15, dir15, who15, pcp15, pwho15] = f_flash(n15, e15, y15)
[on5m, dir5m, who5m, pcp5m, pwho5m] = f_flash(n5m, e5m, y5m)
[on1m, dir1m, who1m, pcp1m, pwho1m] = f_flash(n1m, e1m, y1m)
[on15p, dir15p, who15p] = f_flashP(y15, z15)
[on5mp, dir5mp, who5mp] = f_flashP(y5m, z5m)

// The fast swing candle's own open, without another series: the current bar
// of that timeframe, two bars back. 1m, 5m and 15m bars sit on whole multiples
// of their length from the epoch, and on a closed market the last bar's close
// stands in for "now".
nowT  = math.min(timenow, time_close)
sw1T  = math.floor((nowT - 1) / 60000) * 60000 - 120000
sw5T  = math.floor((nowT - 1) / 300000) * 300000 - 600000
sw15T = math.floor((nowT - 1) / 900000) * 900000 - 1800000
[c1x, q1m]  = f_cyc(sw1T,  i_qt_on ? 1 : 0)
[c5x, q5m]  = f_cyc(sw5T,  i_qt_on ? 2 : 0)
[c15x, q15] = f_cyc(sw15T, i_qt_on ? 3 : 0)

// A fast PSP born in Q1 / a blocked time does not exist when the setting says
// so — not in the box, not in the alert, not in the hub.
on15g  = on15  and not (q1Drop and q15)
on5mg  = on5m  and not (q1Drop and q5m)
on1mg  = on1m  and not (q1Drop and q1m)
on15pg = on15p and not (q1Drop and q15)
on5mpg = on5mp and not (q1Drop and q5m)

// Kept as one-line statements on purpose: Pine treats a continuation line
// indented by any multiple of four spaces as the start of a block, so a
// column-aligned wrapped ternary is a syntax error waiting to happen.
mtfTop = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.top_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.top_center : position.top_right
mtfMid = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.middle_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.middle_center : position.middle_right
mtfBot = i_mtf_h == "שמאל" ? position.bottom_left : i_mtf_h == "מרכז" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right
mtfPos = i_mtf_v == "למעלה" ? mtfTop : i_mtf_v == "באמצע" ? mtfMid : mtfBot

// Padding: empty spacer rows on the edge side push the content away from it.
mtfUp  = i_mtf_v == "למעלה"
mtfRow = mtfUp ? i_mtf_pad : 0

// One cell per entry, because a cell carries a single text colour.
var table mtfTbl = table.new(mtfPos, 18, 1 + i_mtf_pad, border_width = 0)

c_clear = color.new(color.black, 100)

f_put(int col, string tx, color c) =>
    table.cell(mtfTbl, col, mtfRow, tx, text_color = c, text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = c_clear)
    col + 1

if barstate.islast and i_mtf_on
    if i_mtf_pad > 0
        for k = 0 to i_mtf_pad - 1
            table.cell(mtfTbl, 0, mtfUp ? k : 1 + k, " ",
                 text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = c_clear)

    anything = r1w != "" or r1d != "" or r4h != "" or r1h != "" or rCh != "" or rp1w != "" or rp1d != "" or rp4h != "" or rp1h != "" or rpCh != ""
    table.cell(mtfTbl, 0, mtfRow, anything ? "ADI" : "", text_color = i_col_neut,
         text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = c_clear)

    col = 1
    if r1w != ""
        col := f_put(col, r1w, f_col(st1w))
        if d1w
            col := f_put(col, "◦1W", i_col_pend)
    if rp1w != ""
        col := f_put(col, rp1w, f_col(ps1w))
    if r1d != ""
        col := f_put(col, r1d, f_col(st1d))
        if d1d
            col := f_put(col, "◦1D", i_col_pend)
    if rp1d != ""
        col := f_put(col, rp1d, f_col(ps1d))
    if r4h != ""
        col := f_put(col, r4h, f_col(st4h))
        if d4h
            col := f_put(col, "◦4H", i_col_pend)
    if rp4h != ""
        col := f_put(col, rp4h, f_col(ps4h))
    if r1h != ""
        col := f_put(col, r1h, f_col(st1h))
        if d1h
            col := f_put(col, "◦1H", i_col_pend)
    if rp1h != ""
        col := f_put(col, rp1h, f_col(ps1h))
    if rCh != ""
        col := f_put(col, rCh, f_col(stCh))
        if dCh
            col := f_put(col, "◦" + chName, i_col_pend)
    if rpCh != ""
        col := f_put(col, rpCh, f_col(psCh))
    if col <= 17
        for k = col to 17
            table.cell(mtfTbl, k, mtfRow, "", bgcolor = c_clear)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE FAST NOTICE  —  5m / 15m, in a box of its own
//
//  A PSP is a function of three bars and a PCP of one, so both can be read
//  straight off the last bar with nothing accumulated across history. The
//  notice is replaced wholesale at the next close of ITS OWN timeframe.
//  The pair has its own rows, in the pair colour.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

psp15  = i_fast_on and on15g
psp5m  = i_fast_on and on5mg
psp15p = i_fast_on and on15pg
psp5mp = i_fast_on and on5mpg
pnd15  = i_fast_on and i_fast_pcp and pcp15 and not on15
pnd5m  = i_fast_on and i_fast_pcp and pcp5m and not on5m

f15  = psp15 ? "⚡ PSP 15m " + (dir15 < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who15 : pnd15 ? "◦ PCP 15m " + pwho15 : i_fast_idle ? "15m —" : ""
f5m  = psp5m ? "⚡ PSP 5m " + (dir5m < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who5m : pnd5m ? "◦ PCP 5m " + pwho5m : i_fast_idle ? "5m —" : ""
f15p = psp15p ? "⚡ PSP 15m " + (dir15p < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who15p : ""
f5mp = psp5mp ? "⚡ PSP 5m " + (dir5mp < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + " " + who5mp : ""

f_fcol(bool q, int d) =>
    q ? i_col_q1 : d < 0 ? i_col_bear : i_col_bull

fc15  = psp15 ? f_fcol(q15 and q1Col, dir15) : i_col_pend
fc5m  = psp5m ? f_fcol(q5m and q1Col, dir5m) : i_col_pend
fc15p = q15 and q1Col ? i_col_q1 : i_col_pair
fc5mp = q5m and q1Col ? i_col_q1 : i_col_pair

// The tint is what makes it read as a notice. Only a PSP gets one.
fb15  = i_fast_bg and psp15  ? color.new(fc15, 82)  : c_clear
fb5m  = i_fast_bg and psp5m  ? color.new(fc5m, 82)  : c_clear
fb15p = i_fast_bg and psp15p ? color.new(fc15p, 82) : c_clear
fb5mp = i_fast_bg and psp5mp ? color.new(fc5mp, 82) : c_clear

// One-line statements on purpose — see the note above mtfTop.
fastTop = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.top_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.top_center : position.top_right
fastMid = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.middle_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.middle_center : position.middle_right
fastBot = i_fast_h == "שמאל" ? position.bottom_left : i_fast_h == "מרכז" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right
fastPos = i_fast_v == "למעלה" ? fastTop : i_fast_v == "באמצע" ? fastMid : fastBot
fastSz  = i_fast_sz == "קטן" ? size.small : i_fast_sz == "רגיל" ? size.normal : i_fast_sz == "ענק" ? size.huge : size.large

fastUp = i_fast_v == "למעלה"
fastR0 = fastUp ? i_fast_pad : 0

var table fastTbl = table.new(fastPos, 1, 4 + i_fast_pad, border_width = 0)

if barstate.islast and i_fast_on
    if i_fast_pad > 0
        for k = 0 to i_fast_pad - 1
            table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastUp ? k : 4 + k, " ",
                 text_size = size.small, bgcolor = c_clear)

    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0, f15, text_color = fc15,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb15)
    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0 + 1, f15p, text_color = fc15p,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb15p)
    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0 + 2, f5m, text_color = fc5m,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb5m)
    table.cell(fastTbl, 0, fastR0 + 3, f5mp, text_color = fc5mp,
         text_size = fastSz, bgcolor = fb5mp)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALERTS
//  A new break only — never an update to one that exists, never one coming
//  back after a newer one was taken, never what is already there at load
//  (alert() only fires on realtime bars). Short: timeframe and direction,
//  and the pair's names when it is the pair.
//  NOTE: create the alert on the indicator with "Any alert() function call".
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

pairTag = " " + nmY + "/" + nmR

f_nw(MtfSt s, bool on, string nm, bool pair) =>
    on and s.isNew ? nm + " " + f_arrow(s) + (pair ? pairTag : "") : ""

f_add(string a, string b) =>
    a == "" ? b : b == "" ? a : a + "  ·  " + b

newTx = f_nw(st1w, sh1w, "1W", false)
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(ps1w, usePair and sh1w, "1W", true))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(st1d, sh1d, "1D", false))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(ps1d, usePair and sh1d, "1D", true))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(st4h, sh4h, "4H", false))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(ps4h, usePair and sh4h, "4H", true))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(st1h, sh1h, "1H", false))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(ps1h, usePair and sh1h, "1H", true))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(stCh, tf_allowed and chIsBig, chName, false))
newTx := f_add(newTx, f_nw(psCh, usePair and tf_allowed and chIsBig, chName, true))

if i_mtf_alert and i_mtf_on and newTx != ""
    alert("ADI PSP: " + newTx, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// The fast notice, once per CHART bar at most.
fastTx = psp5m ? "5m " + (dir5m < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") : ""
if psp5mp
    fastTx := f_add(fastTx, "5m " + (dir5mp < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + pairTag)
if psp15
    fastTx := f_add(fastTx, "15m " + (dir15 < 0 ? "▼" : "▲"))
if psp15p
    fastTx := f_add(fastTx, "15m " + (dir15p < 0 ? "▼" : "▲") + pairTag)

if i_fast_on and i_fast_alert and fastTx != ""
    alert("ADI PSP: " + fastTx, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  EXPORT TO THE HUB  (QT Hub)
//
//  Two hidden numbers (data window only) the hub reads via input.source.
//  For each timeframe on the ladder 4H · 1H · 15m · 5m · 1m: four digits,
//  two for the newest live bearish PSP and two for the bullish one. In each
//  pair: the kind (1 = PSP, 2 = PSP from asset-3 weakness) and an identity
//  digit.
//    9999 = this timeframe cannot be read from the current chart
//  4H and 1H come from the triad's stepped stacks, so they are alive until
//  taken or their container ends. 15m, 5m and 1m come from the fast reader:
//  a PSP there stands until the next close of its timeframe. The 3–4 pair is
//  not exported. A Q1 / blocked PSP that "does not exist" is not exported
//  either. The full layout is in qt-system/docs/HUB.md and must match the hub.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// The newest live break in one direction — the stack is newest first.
f_hxStk(array<Brk> st, int d, int tfMs) =>
    int  v = 0
    bool f = false
    if array.size(st) > 0
        for k = 0 to array.size(st) - 1
            Brk b = array.get(st, k)
            if not f and b.dir == d
                f := true
                v := (b.weak ? 2 : 1) * 10 + int(math.floor(nz(b.born) / tfMs)) % 10
    v

f_hxFast(bool on, int dir) =>
    (on and dir < 0 ? 10 : 0) * 100 + (on and dir > 0 ? 10 : 0)

hx4h = sh4h ? f_hxStk(b4h, -1, 14400000) * 100 + f_hxStk(b4h, 1, 14400000) : 9999
hx1h = sh1h ? f_hxStk(b1h, -1, 3600000) * 100 + f_hxStk(b1h, 1, 3600000) : 9999
hx15 = f_hxFast(on15g, dir15)
hx5m = f_hxFast(on5mg, dir5m)
hx1m = f_hxFast(on1mg, dir1m)

hubA = 310000000000000.0 + hx4h * 100000000.0 + hx1h * 10000.0 + hx15
hubB = 320000000000000.0 + hx5m * 100000000.0 + hx1m * 10000.0
plot(hubA, "HUB · ADI · A", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.data_window, editable = false)
plot(hubB, "HUB · ADI · B", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.data_window, editable = false)

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  END OF SCRIPT
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
